  "body": "The [example from the introduction](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/dev/introduction.html#a-quick-introduction-to-html) does not have a [character encoding declaration](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#charset). Although the character encoding declaration is not necessary in all circumstances, it would be helpful to include it here to better illustrate a strictly conforming HTML document.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<html lang=\"en\">\r\n <head>\r\n+ <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\r\n  <title>Sample page</title>\r\n </head>\r\n <body>\r\n  <h1>Sample page</h1>\r\n  <p>This is a <a href=\"demo.html\">simple</a> sample.</p>\r\n  <!-- this is a comment -->\r\n </body>\r\n</html>\r\n```",
